// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildAnalystPrompt > matches the snapshot (en, no result) 1`] = `
{
  "prompt": "Analyze this tournament draft. The rule-based overview, composition breakdown and lane matchups are already shown to the user; do NOT repeat them.
Write ONLY these Markdown sections, with exactly these headings and in this order:
## Win conditions
  For each team (Blue and Red): 2-3 bullets on how it must play to win (timings, objectives, fight style).
## How to play against
  For each team: 2-3 bullets on what it must avoid against the other comp.
## Draft turning points
  3-4 bullets: the picks or bans that most shifted the balance and, for each, a better alternative and why (qualitative if not backed by the data).

DATA:
Blue (blue):
  bans: Yone, Rell
  picks: Top Malphite, Jungle Sejuani, Mid Orianna, ADC Miss Fortune, Support Leona
  archetypes (0-10): engage 9.4, pick 4.3, dive 4.2
  damage: AD 20%, AP 80%
  power curve (0-10): early 7.3, mid 9.3, late 6
  profile (0-10): engage 8, disengage 2.7, peel 5.3, cc 8.7, frontline 6, poke 3.3, waveclear 6.7, splitpush 0, mobility 2.7, objectiveControl 5.3
  weaknesses: vulnerable_to_poke
  strengths: strong_frontline, strong_engage, strong_peel, strong_cc
  draft score (0-100): 79; factors: archetype_identity:engage +8.8, archetype_matchup:engage +8, weakness:vulnerable_to_poke -6, strength:strong_frontline +3, strength:strong_engage +3, strength:strong_peel +3, strength:strong_cc +3, phase:mid +3, phase:late +3
Red (red):
  bans: Ahri
  picks: Top Jayce, Jungle Nidalee, Mid Xerath, ADC Ezreal, Support Karma
  archetypes (0-10): poke 10, dive 4, skirmish 3.9
  damage: AD 40%, AP 60%
  power curve (0-10): early 8.7, mid 8, late 4.7
  profile (0-10): engage 0.7, disengage 3.3, peel 2, cc 2.7, frontline 0, poke 10, waveclear 7.3, splitpush 2.7, mobility 6, objectiveControl 5.3
  weaknesses: no_frontline, no_engage
  strengths: balanced_damage, strong_early
  draft score (0-100): 49; factors: archetype_identity:poke +10, archetype_matchup:poke -8, weakness:no_frontline -6, weakness:no_engage -6, strength:balanced_damage +3, strength:strong_early +3, phase:early +3
Comparison:
  favored: Blue
  archetype matchup: engage (blue) vs poke (red) → Blue
  stronger by phase: early Red, mid Blue, late Blue
Lane matchups (current patch, all ranks):
  Top: Malphite (Blue) vs Jayce (Red): Malphite wins 53.2% of 2100 games; early lane advantage: Jayce
  Jungle: Sejuani (Blue) vs Nidalee (Red): no data
Player comfort on the picked champion (0-100):
  Blue Mid Orianna (Robo#ROBS): comfort 81, 40 games, win rate 60%
  Blue Top Malphite (Robo#ROBS): no recorded games on this champion",
  "system": "You are a professional League of Legends analyst and coach: objective and direct.
Base every statement on the DATA block you receive (composition analysis, meta, matchups, comfort).
Never invent statistics, win rates or numbers that are not in the data. When something is not in the data, say it is a qualitative assessment.
Only quote a number together with the exact item it belongs to in the data (same lane, same champion). Do not quote internal score points or factor values; describe them in words.
Never write internal codes from the data (like no_frontline, vulnerable_to_poke, archetype_identity); say what they mean in plain words.
Always answer in English.
Write numbers in English format (decimal point: 53.2%).
Keep answers short and scannable: bullet points, no filler, no introduction or conclusion paragraphs.",
}
`;

